Subject: [PATCH] base-files: skip the trymode bookkeeping on boards without /proc/boot_info

The trymodedone init script that the QSDK patch queue adds to base-files
is written for the Qualcomm reference boards.  It reads the trymode and
bootconfig health interfaces before it looks at the board name, and on
the SBE1V1K (board spectrum,sbe1v1k) none of them exist.  The v89-2 boot
log has eight failing reads and four empty-value compares from it:

  procd: /etc/rc.d/S98trymodedone: cat: can't open
      '/proc/upgrade_info/trymode_inprogress': No such file or directory
  ... bootconfig0/age, bootconfig1/age, bootconfig0/health_status,
      bootconfig1/health_status, bootconfig0/age, bootconfig1/age,
      active_bootconfig: same
  procd: /etc/rc.d/S98trymodedone: sh: out of range   (x4)

The four "out of range" lines come from Bank_health_check(): age0/age1
are empty, so `[ "$BC0_age" -gt "$BC1_age" ]` and the ipq5424 path's
`[ ... -eq ... ]` compare with nothing.

Every branch below needs one of two interfaces: /proc/boot_info (the
reference-board and ipq54xx paths) or /sys/class/registers/bootcount
(the ipq52xx/ipq96xx path).  Return right away when both are absent,
after the milestone-bit write that start() performs for all boards.
Reads that remain keep their diagnostics off, so a partial interface on
a real reference board no longer floods the log either.

On a reference board the branches run exactly as before.

---

--- a/openwrt-patches/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/trymodedone	2026-11-16 02:22:25.098876372 +0000
+++ b/openwrt-patches/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/trymodedone	2026-11-16 02:23:10.967740180 +0000
@@ -138,15 +138,25 @@
 }
 
 start() {
-	local trymode_inprogress="/proc/upgrade_info/trymode_inprogress"
 	local board=$(board_name)
-	local is_in_trymode=$(cat /proc/upgrade_info/trymode_inprogress)
-	local ipq54xx_trymode=$(cat /sys/devices/platform/firmware:scm/trymode_inprogress)
-	local age0=$(cat /proc/boot_info/bootconfig0/age)
-	local age1=$(cat /proc/boot_info/bootconfig1/age)
 
 	#clearing milestone bit
 	echo 0 > /sys/devices/platform/firmware:scm/hlos_done
+
+	# The trymode bookkeeping below only exists on the QCA reference boards.
+	# On any other board the reads fail with "No such file or directory", and
+	# the empty values then turn into four "out of range" compares on every
+	# boot.  The two interfaces tested here are exactly what the branches
+	# below need, so there is nothing to do when both are absent.
+	if [ ! -d /proc/boot_info ] && [ ! -f /sys/class/registers/bootcount ]; then
+		return 0
+	fi
+
+	local trymode_inprogress="/proc/upgrade_info/trymode_inprogress"
+	local is_in_trymode=$(cat /proc/upgrade_info/trymode_inprogress 2>/dev/null)
+	local ipq54xx_trymode=$(cat /sys/devices/platform/firmware:scm/trymode_inprogress 2>/dev/null)
+	local age0=$(cat /proc/boot_info/bootconfig0/age 2>/dev/null)
+	local age1=$(cat /proc/boot_info/bootconfig1/age 2>/dev/null)
 	case "$board" in
 		qcom,ipq9574-ap-al05 |\
 		qcom,ipq9574-ap-al06 |\
